# --- Corpus and artifacts (never committed; §6.3 release policy is code + manifest only)
# Leading slash matters: a bare `data/` also matches ravaan/data/ and configs/data/, which would
# silently drop the corpus pipeline source from the repo.
# Trailing `*` matters too: git cannot re-include a file whose *parent directory* is excluded,
# so `/data/` + `!/data/manifest.json` silently ignores the negation. `/data/*` excludes the
# entries rather than the directory, which is what makes the exceptions below work.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
!/data/manifest.json
# ...and §7's tokenizer, which is an instrument rather than corpus — the sixth thing this file's
# leading `/data/*` would have silently dropped. 302 KB of model, and the packed corpus is an
# undecodable array of integers without it; §4.1 requires the *same* tokenizer for every model in
# the comparison, so "which tokenizer was this" must never be a question about a local file.
# Re-including a directory takes two lines, not one: `/data/*` excludes the `tokenizer` entry
# itself, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded (same trap as
# `/data/` vs `/data/*` above). So: re-include the directory, exclude its contents, then name the
# artifacts. The 46 MB of `sample_*.txt` it was trained from stays out — that is corpus.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v data/tokenizer/ravaan-16k.model` (reports nothing) and
# `git check-ignore -v data/tokenizer/sample_urdu.txt` (still ignored).
!/data/tokenizer/
/data/tokenizer/*
!/data/tokenizer/*.model
!/data/tokenizer/*.vocab
!/data/tokenizer/*.json
/data/raw/
/checkpoints/
/runs/
/logs/
wandb/
*.arrow
*.parquet
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.zst
# ...except the ones under reports/, which are evidence rather than corpus. The stage-5
# validation sample is a .jsonl and the review sheet beside it is useless without it — the
# `score` command reads the metrics from here. Third time a blanket ignore has nearly dropped
# something load-bearing (session 2's bare `data/`, session 4's `/data/`), so: verified with
# `git check-ignore -v reports/quality_sample.jsonl`, which now reports nothing.
# Session 17 re-included `/reports/freeze/*.jsonl` as a second one-level negation, and session 18
# found the fifth instance the moment it wrote `reports/eval/`. A negation per subdirectory is the
# bug, not the fix: `**` re-includes evidence at any depth, and no future report directory has to
# remember this file exists. Verified with `git check-ignore -v reports/eval/pairs_testsplit_roman.jsonl`.
!/reports/**/*.jsonl
# Detached-run scratch: console logs (`nohup … > reports/.decon_wiki.log`) and completion
# sentinels (`touch reports/.subs_done`). Not evidence — the evidence is the JSON the run writes.
# The rule was `.*.log` and session 21 arrived with a `.subs_done` it did not match, so it is
# widened to the class it was always about: dot-prefixed is the convention for transient here, and
# no report is named with a leading dot. Verified with `git check-ignore -v reports/.subs_done`.
/reports/.*
*.txt.zst
*.model
*.vocab
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.npy
# §7's tokenizer, re-included *here* rather than beside the `/data/` block above, because the last
# matching pattern wins and `*.model`/`*.vocab` are three lines up. Placing the negation next to
# what it is arguing with is the seventh instance of this file's recurring bug and the first one
# caught by its own verification line instead of by a missing file weeks later.
!/data/tokenizer/*.model
!/data/tokenizer/*.vocab

